[1m[38;5;231mHow should a user be identified in log records?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mCorrelation ID (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mPer-session random ID. Trace one session end to end; log store never becomes an account list.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Hashed username
     [38;5;246mStable hash links a user's sessions over time. More debugging power, still not plaintext — but it is durable [39m
     [38;5;246mpseudonymous PII.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Raw username
     [38;5;246mMost convenient for support ('find user X's failures'). Puts real account identifiers in your log store.[39m
